{
  "id": 3001,
  "name": "CHEFS submission review and resubmission",
  "description": "## What it does\n\nReceives a CHEFS Event Subscription webhook, fetches the full submission, and asks a reviewer to approve it or request changes through the Workflow Interaction Layer. Approval sends a confirmation email. A change request emails the submitter a recall link, waits for resubmission, fetches the updated data, and returns it to the reviewer in the same execution.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Select the same **Header Auth** credential on **CHEFS Event** and **CHEFS Resubmit Wait**, with Name `x-n8n-chef-key` and a long random Value.\n2. Select a **CHEFS Form Authentication** credential on both extractor nodes.\n3. Select a **Workflow Interaction Layer API** credential on **Reviewer Decision** and an **SMTP** credential on both email nodes.\n4. In **Build Review Context**, replace `submission.data.fullName` and `submission.data.email` with the form's field API names.\n5. Set the reviewer group, role, or user on **Reviewer Decision**.\n6. In CHEFS, enable Event Subscription and Recall Submission. Set Endpoint URL to `/rest/custom/v1/chefs/trip-plan` on this n8n host, Key to `x-n8n-chef-key`, and Endpoint Token to the Header Auth value.\n7. Activate the workflow before submitting the form.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe Webhook path is `trip-plan`; change it in both the Webhook node and CHEFS Endpoint URL if it is already in use. Use the platform `/rest/custom/v1/chefs/...` endpoint rather than the direct n8n webhook so resubmissions can resume the waiting execution. No credentials or pinned execution data are included.",
